Bypass, and Saskatoon’s Circle Drive are some examples of freeways. Entering a freeway The key to entering a freeway is to increase your speed in the acceleration lane until it matches the speed of the vehicles already on the freeway. You also need to plan your merge: 1. While on the entrance ramp, look at the freeway traffic and determine where you want to merge. 2. Build up your speed in the acceleration lane as quickly as you can. 3. Continue to check the spot where you want to merge. 4. Signal, make your final shoulder check and accelerate into the freeway lane. Merging at less than freeway speeds can be dangerous. While on the freeway The left lane is specifically for passing slower vehicles—not for regular driving—while the right lane is for normal travel. However, at times you may need to move into the centre or left lanes temporarily to allow other drivers
